  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Missing end-to-end handoff",
      "items": [
        "No code passes segmentation predictions into the prescription-map generator.",
        "Path-planning experiments do not read the generated map files; the controller does not read route output.",
        "Cell 21 saved output identifies torchvision DeepLabV3-ResNet50 loaded through torch.hub. The separate checked-in ResNet101 model definition is unused in that saved run."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Split and artifact distinctions",
      "items": [
        "Notebook cell 5 writes split_data/train.txt and test.txt from list_of_images.txt. Dataset cell 20 instead reads train_et.txt/test_et.txt created by cell 18; this ET pair is missing here.",
        "loss.png shows 75 iterations, while cell 21 performs 400 updates and comments out its save call; it is from a different, unrecorded run. crop6GT.png is a full-field sugarcane ground-truth label map used as input to rotation and tiling.",
        "Stored notebook outputs and images do not prove this checkout reruns successfully.",
        "Cell 21 updates the model on test_loader; cell 22 metrics therefore describe a contaminated test set, not an unbiased generalization estimate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Input and target encoding caveats",
      "items": [
        "Cell 20 computes RGB-derived ExG/ExGR/CIVE expressions in uint8, then casts to float32; overflow happens first. The model input is wrapped RGB encoding, not mathematically correct floating-point indices.",
        "Cell 20 recolors WeedMap red pixels yellow and black pixels red, then constructs two target channels. Under this visible encoding, weed pixels match neither target color, become [0,0], and argmax maps the tie to class 0 (weed); class 1 is crop + soil/background. This implementation-dependent behavior is not an intentional class encoding. The create_mask helper is missing from this checkout."
      ]
    }
  ]
